1
00:00:23,791 --> 00:00:26,041
Come on.

2
00:00:27,081 --> 00:00:29,631
Come on.

3
00:00:32,381 --> 00:00:34,131
Hey. It's a warship.

4
00:00:34,801 --> 00:00:36,091
Tell Gorm. Hurry.

5
00:00:36,761 --> 00:00:38,761
Wait. Look closely.

6
00:00:39,811 --> 00:00:41,521
They're Askeladd's ships.

7
00:00:48,521 --> 00:00:51,531
We finally made it back to the village.

8
00:00:52,031 --> 00:00:54,741
Well, we survived another year.

9
00:00:54,821 --> 00:00:57,491
And you still haven't died, Bjorn.

10
00:00:57,571 --> 00:01:00,371
We went pretty far.

11
00:01:00,451 --> 00:01:01,291
What?

12
00:01:02,201 --> 00:01:05,371
Hey. It's the sheep. They're still grazing them.

13
00:01:06,461 --> 00:01:09,131
They're trying to fatten them up.

14
00:01:09,211 --> 00:01:12,841
It looks like Gorm's still stingy as usual.

15
00:01:21,351 --> 00:01:22,601
Men.

16
00:01:22,681 --> 00:01:24,641
Thanks for your hard work this year.

17
00:01:24,731 --> 00:01:27,191
Enjoy the winter.

18
00:03:07,081 --> 00:03:08,041
Over there.

19
00:03:09,251 --> 00:03:10,211
NOVEMBER 1012 AD

20
00:03:10,291 --> 00:03:12,831
FEUDAL LORD GORM'S VILLAGE
JUTLAND PENINSULA

21
00:03:13,881 --> 00:03:16,001
There's so much treasure.

22
00:03:16,671 --> 00:03:18,761
They had a huge victory
in the land of the Franks.

23
00:03:18,841 --> 00:03:20,131
BEYOND THE EDGE OF THE SEA

24
00:03:20,221 --> 00:03:21,261
I'm impressed, Askeladd.

25
00:03:21,761 --> 00:03:24,681
-I heard some men died this year.
-Really?

26
00:03:24,761 --> 00:03:27,391
I wonder if they're going to look for new sailors again.

27
00:03:28,221 --> 00:03:30,021
Damn. I can't wait.

28
00:03:30,101 --> 00:03:32,731
If I'm going to sail, I want to sail with Askeladd.

29
00:03:32,811 --> 00:03:35,981
Idiot. You'd die within three days.

30
00:03:41,201 --> 00:03:43,321
Hey. Say you're sorry.

31
00:03:56,291 --> 00:03:57,921
What's wrong with that kid?

32
00:04:04,051 --> 00:04:06,601
Ready? One, two...

33
00:04:07,141 --> 00:04:09,221
Askeladd.

34
00:04:09,311 --> 00:04:11,351
Welcome home.

35
00:04:11,891 --> 00:04:14,231
Hey, girls.

36
00:04:14,311 --> 00:04:15,901
You're so cute.

37
00:04:16,561 --> 00:04:19,651
Hey. I brought you some necklaces.

38
00:04:21,651 --> 00:04:23,151
-I'll take it.
-I want a ring.

39
00:04:24,031 --> 00:04:25,531
Hey, Uncle Gorm.

40
00:04:25,611 --> 00:04:29,541
The girls here aren't modest at all. It's wonderful.

41
00:04:30,081 --> 00:04:32,451
I'm here to talk about a serious matter.

42
00:04:32,541 --> 00:04:33,661
Are you ready to listen?

43
00:04:34,291 --> 00:04:35,121
Listen.

44
00:04:35,211 --> 00:04:37,841
The cost to feed one of your men

45
00:04:37,921 --> 00:04:40,551
is one and one-fourth silver coins per day.

46
00:04:41,211 --> 00:04:43,511
You have 97 men,

47
00:04:43,591 --> 00:04:45,761
so that's 121 coins in total--

48
00:04:45,841 --> 00:04:48,141
You want to talk about money again?

49
00:04:48,221 --> 00:04:50,681
The price of pork increased this year.

50
00:04:50,761 --> 00:04:53,431
If you want to eat pork every day,
then you would need...

51
00:04:54,101 --> 00:04:55,771
Beer is charged separately.

52
00:04:55,851 --> 00:04:58,231
And if you add in the cost of lodging and firewood...

53
00:04:58,311 --> 00:05:00,861
Uncle, stop worrying.

54
00:05:00,941 --> 00:05:02,571
We earned a lot this year.

55
00:05:03,031 --> 00:05:06,451
Give my men plenty of booze and food.

56
00:05:06,531 --> 00:05:08,241
I'll pay.

57
00:05:08,321 --> 00:05:10,991
That's what I was waiting to hear.

58
00:05:11,081 --> 00:05:12,081
I'll buy you a drink.

59
00:05:12,621 --> 00:05:14,081
Bring the celebratory drinks.

60
00:05:14,161 --> 00:05:16,831
We have some good wine, right? Bring it here.

61
00:05:18,251 --> 00:05:20,421
One, two, three...

62
00:05:20,501 --> 00:05:23,011
Uncle. Do you really love money so much?

63
00:05:24,051 --> 00:05:25,921
Is there anyone who doesn't?

64
00:05:26,511 --> 00:05:30,601
Money is great. Just looking at it makes me happy.

65
00:05:34,351 --> 00:05:36,691
Hey, Hordaland. What are you doing?

66
00:05:37,351 --> 00:05:39,231
Hurry up, and bring the wine.

67
00:05:41,571 --> 00:05:42,401
Yes, sir.

68
00:05:43,901 --> 00:05:46,071
Oh, dear. What a troublesome woman.

69
00:05:48,661 --> 00:05:50,281
What a weird name.

70
00:05:50,371 --> 00:05:53,831
That slave girl. Hordaland?

71
00:05:53,911 --> 00:05:56,461
-It's the name of a region in Norway.
-Yeah.

72
00:05:56,541 --> 00:05:58,081
I bought her recently.

73
00:05:58,581 --> 00:06:03,501
She's the daughter of a feudal lord,
but her family lost a battle, and fell to ruin.

74
00:06:05,421 --> 00:06:08,131
She's a beautiful girl, and she was expensive.

75
00:06:08,221 --> 00:06:10,011
But she's slow at work.

76
00:06:10,091 --> 00:06:15,521
Rich girls are useless.
They just have a lot of pride.

77
00:06:16,561 --> 00:06:18,601
-By the way, Uncle...
-What?

78
00:06:18,691 --> 00:06:20,651
Can I ask you to be my witness?

79
00:06:21,401 --> 00:06:24,481
I'm scheduled for a duel before dinner.

80
00:06:24,571 --> 00:06:25,531
A duel?

81
00:06:25,611 --> 00:06:26,861
And...

82
00:06:28,491 --> 00:06:31,491
It's not the slave's fault that she's useless.

83
00:06:31,571 --> 00:06:33,741
You're just bad at using her.

84
00:06:33,831 --> 00:06:34,911
What did you say?

85
00:06:37,161 --> 00:06:38,541
You can make use of anyone...

86
00:06:39,541 --> 00:06:42,381
with the right approach.

87
00:06:45,051 --> 00:06:45,921
What?

88
00:06:46,001 --> 00:06:46,961
What's going on?

89
00:06:47,051 --> 00:06:48,551
It's a duel.

90
00:06:48,631 --> 00:06:50,301
You can do it, kid.

91
00:06:50,381 --> 00:06:52,681
Do it. Don't lose to him.

92
00:06:56,561 --> 00:07:00,601
In the name of Odin,

93
00:07:00,691 --> 00:07:04,021
the duel between Thorfinn
and Askeladd is about to begin.

94
00:07:04,691 --> 00:07:07,401
Each man may choose their own weapon.

95
00:07:07,481 --> 00:07:09,281
If you fight with honor,

96
00:07:09,361 --> 00:07:14,531
your soul shall pass through the gates of Valhalla,
even if you shall die.

97
00:07:15,031 --> 00:07:16,411
Seriously?

98
00:07:16,491 --> 00:07:18,751
He's one of Askeladd's men?

99
00:07:19,501 --> 00:07:22,371
Maybe he'd let even someone
like me sail with him too.

100
00:07:23,001 --> 00:07:26,041
-He's kind of cute, right?
-What?

101
00:07:26,131 --> 00:07:29,011
Askeladd has more money. And he's strong.

102
00:07:29,551 --> 00:07:34,891
The reason for this duel is for Thorfinn
to avenge his father's death.

103
00:07:35,971 --> 00:07:38,641
-Are there any objections?
-No.

104
00:07:39,311 --> 00:07:40,271
No.

105
00:07:41,441 --> 00:07:43,101
Then begin.

106
00:07:46,731 --> 00:07:49,651
Unbelievable. Thorfinn's so stubborn.

107
00:07:54,991 --> 00:07:55,821
Go.

108
00:07:55,911 --> 00:07:57,081
You can do it.

109
00:07:57,161 --> 00:07:58,621
Do it.

110
00:07:58,701 --> 00:07:59,791
You...

111
00:08:00,831 --> 00:08:02,831
got taller.

112
00:08:02,921 --> 00:08:04,331
How old are you now?

113
00:08:08,091 --> 00:08:09,841
You were still only this tall back then--

114
00:08:14,131 --> 00:08:15,011
Thorfinn attacked.

115
00:08:16,011 --> 00:08:17,261
He got up close.

116
00:08:19,811 --> 00:08:22,731
You should go along with making small-talk...

117
00:08:23,981 --> 00:08:25,601
with old men.

118
00:08:31,031 --> 00:08:33,031
-He got up.
-He's okay.

119
00:08:34,111 --> 00:08:36,321
He sent him flying with a single hit.

120
00:08:36,411 --> 00:08:39,031
Idiot. Thorfinn jumped.

121
00:08:39,701 --> 00:08:42,911
He knows that the one with the dagger has the advantage
at close range.

122
00:08:44,081 --> 00:08:45,501
He's stronger now.

123
00:08:46,581 --> 00:08:48,171
-Nice, kid.
-Askeladd.

124
00:08:50,131 --> 00:08:51,511
Do it.

125
00:09:03,521 --> 00:09:04,431
He's good.

126
00:09:12,781 --> 00:09:13,611
Damn.

127
00:09:20,201 --> 00:09:21,541
Nice.

128
00:09:22,621 --> 00:09:23,621
Get him.

129
00:09:24,791 --> 00:09:26,871
Hang in there, kid.

130
00:09:30,671 --> 00:09:31,881
Hey, Thorfinn.

131
00:09:33,461 --> 00:09:37,591
Your father... What was his name?

132
00:09:38,761 --> 00:09:42,641
Tho... Tho... Tho...

133
00:09:42,721 --> 00:09:43,851
It's Thors.

134
00:09:45,431 --> 00:09:48,351
Thors. That's right.

135
00:09:48,441 --> 00:09:51,231
Getting old is making me forgetful.

136
00:09:55,531 --> 00:09:57,401
But you know...

137
00:09:57,491 --> 00:10:03,041
I know you're in the middle of getting revenge,
so I feel bad saying this.

138
00:10:03,121 --> 00:10:05,661
I've killed a lot of people, you know.

139
00:10:05,751 --> 00:10:09,541
I can't quite remember your father.

140
00:10:10,671 --> 00:10:13,251
Did I really kill him?

141
00:10:13,341 --> 00:10:15,301
Did I kill Thoril?

142
00:10:16,341 --> 00:10:20,051
Hey. Do you remember how I killed him?

143
00:10:20,141 --> 00:10:21,301
What if...?

144
00:10:21,391 --> 00:10:23,851
Well, maybe you're wrong.

145
00:10:25,431 --> 00:10:26,731
You bastard.

146
00:10:27,931 --> 00:10:30,191
If you had fought him with honor,

147
00:10:31,231 --> 00:10:33,941
my father would never have lost to you.

148
00:10:36,031 --> 00:10:38,201
During that fight,

149
00:10:38,281 --> 00:10:39,321
you...

150
00:10:46,451 --> 00:10:48,501
You took me hostage.

151
00:10:48,581 --> 00:10:51,331
Oh, that's right. I remember now.

152
00:10:51,421 --> 00:10:55,211
He's that idiot who put down his sword
to save a kid's life.

153
00:11:13,111 --> 00:11:15,771
What did he do just now?

154
00:11:21,411 --> 00:11:23,491
Don't get so worked up.

155
00:11:23,571 --> 00:11:25,781
You haven't trained enough, kid.

156
00:11:26,951 --> 00:11:29,251
Damn you.

157
00:11:44,391 --> 00:11:46,561
Bjorn. Pick him up.

158
00:11:46,641 --> 00:11:47,681
Sure.

159
00:11:50,021 --> 00:11:51,181
I'm hungry.

160
00:11:51,851 --> 00:11:53,101
Oh, that's right.

161
00:11:54,151 --> 00:11:55,021
Uncle.

162
00:11:56,901 --> 00:12:00,111
I want to eat some lamb breast.

163
00:12:00,191 --> 00:12:01,951
Roasted with herbs.

164
00:12:25,261 --> 00:12:26,761
I've been waiting for this.

165
00:12:31,181 --> 00:12:32,981
It's so cold.

166
00:12:33,061 --> 00:12:35,601
Hey. Aren't you supposed to guard the ship?

167
00:12:35,691 --> 00:12:38,651
I got out of it. Thorfinn said he doesn't want to switch.

168
00:12:39,151 --> 00:12:42,531
You mean he's in a bad mood because he lost?

169
00:12:42,611 --> 00:12:45,781
He's always been like that.

170
00:12:47,121 --> 00:12:49,031
He feels comfortable there.

171
00:12:49,991 --> 00:12:52,411
It used to be his father's ship.

172
00:12:53,461 --> 00:12:54,961
Just leave him alone.

173
00:13:02,461 --> 00:13:04,341
Not bad.

174
00:13:04,421 --> 00:13:05,551
Askeladd.

175
00:13:06,591 --> 00:13:10,101
Today's duel was amazing.

176
00:13:10,181 --> 00:13:11,601
What? Really?

177
00:13:13,231 --> 00:13:15,811
You threw him at the end, right?

178
00:13:15,891 --> 00:13:19,271
How did you do that? That was so cool.

179
00:13:19,941 --> 00:13:21,531
But you know, captain...

180
00:13:21,611 --> 00:13:24,321
Are you sure about taking a kid
like him sailing with you?

181
00:13:24,401 --> 00:13:26,911
What if he attacks you while you sleep?

182
00:13:26,991 --> 00:13:29,121
I'll be fine.

183
00:13:29,201 --> 00:13:31,491
He could never do it.

184
00:13:35,001 --> 00:13:36,581
What do you mean?

185
00:13:36,671 --> 00:13:39,631
He's a warrior, too, you know.

186
00:13:39,711 --> 00:13:43,381
He'd only accept victory with honor.

187
00:13:48,131 --> 00:13:52,221
He's held back by his past, and his pride.

188
00:13:57,691 --> 00:13:59,981
It's you again, Horda.

189
00:14:00,481 --> 00:14:03,231
You're in the way. Clean it up. Hurry.

190
00:14:03,821 --> 00:14:06,491
You're not a noblewoman anymore.

191
00:14:06,571 --> 00:14:09,911
Stand up, you clumsy girl.

192
00:14:09,991 --> 00:14:11,991
I don't get it.

193
00:14:12,621 --> 00:14:14,741
If I had to live without pride,

194
00:14:14,831 --> 00:14:17,161
I'd rather kill myself.

195
00:14:19,751 --> 00:14:22,131
What's wrong? Did I say something funny?

196
00:14:22,211 --> 00:14:24,001
No. It's not you.

197
00:14:28,011 --> 00:14:29,721
Look.

198
00:14:29,801 --> 00:14:32,011
It's terrible.

199
00:14:32,101 --> 00:14:35,101
Don't forget, you're just a slave.

200
00:14:35,181 --> 00:14:37,271
The guy who's a slave to money holds a whip,

201
00:14:37,351 --> 00:14:41,311
and pretends to be the master
of the slave he bought with his money.

202
00:14:43,901 --> 00:14:45,981
He just doesn't realize it himself.

203
00:14:47,031 --> 00:14:50,281
Everyone is a slave to something.

204
00:15:07,261 --> 00:15:08,591
You upset?

205
00:15:16,561 --> 00:15:17,721
Father.

206
00:15:33,451 --> 00:15:37,201
Hey. Crybaby.

207
00:15:47,051 --> 00:15:48,881
Does it hurt, kid?

208
00:15:50,011 --> 00:15:51,631
Do you want to get revenge?

209
00:15:55,601 --> 00:15:57,681
Well, you're my son.

210
00:15:57,761 --> 00:16:01,101
If I told you not to seek revenge, you wouldn't listen.

211
00:16:01,941 --> 00:16:03,521
This is a problem.

212
00:16:04,771 --> 00:16:06,361
I don't know what to say.

213
00:16:08,071 --> 00:16:10,991
Maybe you'll just have to realize it on your own.

214
00:16:13,781 --> 00:16:15,701
I told you, right?

215
00:16:15,781 --> 00:16:18,741
You don't have any enemies.

216
00:16:18,831 --> 00:16:21,161
No one has any enemies.

217
00:16:29,501 --> 00:16:32,631
A true warrior doesn't need a sword...

218
00:16:51,151 --> 00:16:54,111
Master Gorm told me

219
00:16:54,201 --> 00:16:56,201
to bring you some food.

220
00:17:19,301 --> 00:17:22,601
Hey. Are you a slave too?

221
00:17:22,681 --> 00:17:23,891
What?

222
00:17:23,981 --> 00:17:26,601
Well, you're eating out here.

223
00:17:28,351 --> 00:17:30,111
I'm a warrior.

224
00:17:30,191 --> 00:17:31,691
Unlike you,

225
00:17:31,781 --> 00:17:33,991
I can eat wherever I like.

226
00:17:35,071 --> 00:17:36,491
Really?

227
00:17:36,571 --> 00:17:41,121
But I feel like you're the same as me.

228
00:17:42,581 --> 00:17:44,371
I have no idea how a slave feels.

229
00:17:45,121 --> 00:17:50,081
If I were you, I'd kill Gorm and run away.
I'd kill everyone who came after me too.

230
00:17:51,751 --> 00:17:54,341
Kill him? I could never kill someone.

231
00:17:56,471 --> 00:17:58,841
Then you'll be a slave for the rest of your life.

232
00:17:58,931 --> 00:18:00,141
It's your choice.

233
00:18:06,891 --> 00:18:08,271
If I run away...

234
00:18:08,771 --> 00:18:10,771
Run away as far as I can...

235
00:18:10,861 --> 00:18:13,731
If I run away to the other side of the ocean,

236
00:18:13,821 --> 00:18:16,281
then what's there?

237
00:18:19,911 --> 00:18:22,411
There's probably nothing there, right?

238
00:18:23,451 --> 00:18:25,791
No matter how far I go, it'd be the same as here.

239
00:18:25,871 --> 00:18:28,671
Just filled with wars, and slave traders.

240
00:18:46,181 --> 00:18:47,231
Far west,

241
00:18:48,271 --> 00:18:49,601
across the sea,

242
00:18:50,901 --> 00:18:52,231
there is a land called

243
00:18:53,271 --> 00:18:54,231
Vinland.

244
00:18:55,321 --> 00:18:57,191
It's warm.

245
00:18:57,281 --> 00:18:58,741
And fertile.

246
00:18:58,821 --> 00:19:00,491
A faraway land,

247
00:19:00,571 --> 00:19:03,911
where neither slave traders
nor the flames of war reach.

248
00:19:05,831 --> 00:19:08,121
No one would be able

249
00:19:08,201 --> 00:19:09,581
to find you there.

250
00:19:13,501 --> 00:19:16,501
Does such a place truly exist?

251
00:19:52,121 --> 00:19:54,751
AUGUST 1013 AD
VICINITY OF JELLING, DENMARK

252
00:20:00,011 --> 00:20:04,931
The finest warriors
from clans all over Denmark are gathering.

253
00:20:05,471 --> 00:20:06,471
In addition,

254
00:20:06,551 --> 00:20:10,681
four of our Jomsvikings brigades are hastening
to join them.

255
00:20:11,731 --> 00:20:14,151
Everything is proceeding as planned

256
00:20:14,231 --> 00:20:16,151
for the upcoming campaign.

257
00:20:22,701 --> 00:20:24,571
The time has finally come.

258
00:20:24,661 --> 00:20:27,411
We must show those insolent English scoundrels

259
00:20:27,951 --> 00:20:30,371
the power of the king.

260
00:20:31,411 --> 00:20:32,251
Sir.

261
00:20:32,331 --> 00:20:33,671
Yes, sir.

262
00:20:33,751 --> 00:20:38,291
We will fight without yield
to achieve Your Highness's goal of capturing England.

263
00:20:41,211 --> 00:20:43,051
Where's Canute?

264
00:20:43,131 --> 00:20:44,801
He's here, right?

265
00:20:45,221 --> 00:20:46,181
Yes.

266
00:20:46,261 --> 00:20:48,891
His Highness has already arrived in Jelling.

267
00:20:48,971 --> 00:20:52,311
He's resting to prepare to march.

268
00:20:52,391 --> 00:20:56,191
Your Highness. Are you sure,
you don't want to change your mind?

269
00:20:56,271 --> 00:20:57,861
Ragnar.

270
00:20:57,941 --> 00:21:01,071
There's no need for His Highness Canute
to come along.

271
00:21:02,151 --> 00:21:04,861
He's a candidate to succeed the throne.

272
00:21:04,951 --> 00:21:07,491
I must give him a chance
to display valor on the battlefield,

273
00:21:07,571 --> 00:21:09,621
so that he doesn't lose to his brother Harald.

274
00:21:09,701 --> 00:21:14,331
But His Highness doesn't
have much experience on the battlefield.

275
00:21:14,751 --> 00:21:16,581
Ragnar.

276
00:21:16,671 --> 00:21:19,091
I'm worried for Canute's safety as well.

277
00:21:20,131 --> 00:21:23,591
However, we're the leaders of the Vikings.

278
00:21:23,671 --> 00:21:26,591
If we don't demonstrate valor,
the people will not follow us.

279
00:21:28,011 --> 00:21:30,181
We shall sail tomorrow morning.

280
00:21:53,621 --> 00:21:56,871
In August of 1013 AD,

281
00:21:56,961 --> 00:22:01,541
a Danish and Viking fleet, led by King Sweyn,

282
00:22:01,631 --> 00:22:05,381
invaded the northern part of England,
starting from the Humber River.

283
00:22:06,591 --> 00:22:08,381
In the region of Gainsborough,

284
00:22:08,471 --> 00:22:11,351
five major cities were taken,

285
00:22:11,431 --> 00:22:16,931
and the main army continued
their advance south over land with great speed.

286
00:22:17,981 --> 00:22:21,811
They overran the region,
as they continued their advance.

287
00:22:23,941 --> 00:22:30,911
However, their steady advance came
to a temporary halt...

288
00:22:30,991 --> 00:22:32,621
LONDON

289
00:22:32,701 --> 00:22:35,581
at the merchant town of London.

290
00:22:38,161 --> 00:22:41,171
OCTOBER 1013 AD
LONDON, ENGLAND

291
00:23:02,981 --> 00:23:06,941
What's wrong? Bring it on.

292
00:23:07,031 --> 00:23:10,151
This is a fun war.
